Z||000000||SCCA FIERO||12-19-1999||11:33 PM||||I got my new Fiero Store catalog the other day and in it they offer this. It's 3mm larger than stock. Just by looking at the stock unit you can tell it needs to be bigger. Would 3mm make an improvement to justify the $199.95? ($100.00 core)||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||12-19-1999||11:37 PM||||My wife seems to think so.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Shiner||12-19-1999||11:46 PM||||I am by no means an expert on the fiero intake system, but think about this. Unless the throttle body is a restriction in the system (ie, it can't suck enough air through it to operate at it's full potential), then it won't do a damn thing.  If you have some mods, then maybe this bigger TB is justified. Let's wait to hear from the experts on this one  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||12-20-1999||12:46 AM||||No, I wouldn't do it. What fools people is that you get more throttle opening at a lower throttle position. But wide open is nothing different. I *might* consider it on a 3.4L upgrade, but even then I wouldn't expect much change.<P>Think about this. GM gets 160HP and 190 ft-lbs torque from just increasing the bore and stroke over the 2.8L using the 2.8L induction. Gee, GM didn't increase the intake size......<P>TK||||reg||1
